  "body": "The maintainer asked in chat on 2026-11-22 that the option \"Pass starts at: Auto / Inside / Outside\" go to every operation whose passes or rings have an order. The record of his words is on #3316. This issue is the part for **2D Adaptive**.\n\n## What exists\n\nPR #3353 (for #3316) adds the shared parameter for 2D Offset:\n- The type `machining2d::PassStart { Auto, Inside, Outside }` and its ring law `PassStart::rank` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/pass_start.rs`).\n- One project key `pass_start` (`project::PassStartDto`). `auto` is never written.\n- The generic MCP door `edit_operation`, and one Passes-tab row `Pass starts at` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/pass_start_row.rs`).\n- The design is in `docs/decisions/3316-pass-start-shared.md`.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Give 2D Adaptive the field `pass_start` with the same type, key, row and MCP door. Do not make a new type.\n- Make the planner of 2D Adaptive read it. Where to look: the HSM plan in `pocket_hsm.rs` (`hsm_passes`) and its ring fallback (`plan_passes` at `pocket_hsm.rs`), and the trochoidal method in `adaptive_troch*.rs`; the #2849 pin 3 (`shoulder_adaptive::fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`) is the same fig8 Outside case.\n- Auto must keep the current output of 2D Adaptive byte for byte (each golden).\n- If 2D Adaptive has no pass order, its row says so by name, and the issue records why.\n- Leave room for the start point and the exit point of #1448 beside the parameter.\n\n## Safety\n\nThe change can change posted moves. It is under the safety floor. The pin goes red first. The review is an independent read with a hand trace of one level.\n\nDone means: 2D Adaptive has the option in the property panel, in MCP and in the project file; Inside and Outside force the order; Auto keeps all shipped goldens byte-identical; a pin test shows the forced order.\n\nRefs #3316\nRefs #1448\n",
